; Win it low, keep the double. Winning 42 p. 37 (S-0056-a's first rule, try
; to win a trick to get the lead; S-0056-b), p. 40 (S-0061-a, S-0061-b);
; played by the bidder in Hand 23 (S-0105-b).
; Rule, in our words: on the bidder's side, following a suit no setter can
; trump (or playing last), win the trick when you can, and with the lowest
; tile that is sure to win: holding the double and the next-highest tile still
; out, win with the second and keep the double for a lead of your own
; (stretching the double).
; New: no gate has it.

(include book)

(policy helper-stretch
  (rule win-with-the-lowest-sure-tile (play sure)
    (viewer me)
    (or (bidder me) (bidders-partner me))
    (current-winner w)
    (opponent me w)
    (trick-play w win)
    (led-context q)
    (not (trump q))
    (or (no-setter-trump) (last-to-play))
    (follower sure)
    (beats sure win q)
    (not (loses-in sure q))
    (none (roles lower)
      (follower lower)
      (beats lower win q)
      (not (loses-in lower q))
      (beats sure lower q))))
